# DIAGNOSTICS

`vx: remote: the node refused the warm boot` with rc's reason above it; `warmboot ended before the copies were done` when a copy failed, and `without a warm boot` when it failed after them; `no new boot's cpu server on the node 120 s after the copies` when none came back.
It exits 0 when the new boot answers, 1 otherwise.
`vx remote trace` says `trace(8) copied nothing` when the session ended without a recording, trace(8)'s own words above it.
`vx remote test` says `vx remote test: <platform>: passed` or `FAILED:` and why, and exits 0 only when it passed; `can't open <dev>` names the error, and for permission the group to run it in; `--record needs a committed tree`.

# BUGS

The images cross the link at about 120 MB/s under KVM, and much slower without: a 100 MB cpu image takes under a second, or many seconds under TCG.
rc's output on the node reaches this terminal through a ring, so its last lines before the warm boot, `warmboot: handing over` among them, may be lost with the old kernel.
The budgets are printed, not judged: `vx bench` doesn't run them yet.
